+# Edge Case Hunter — Odin Prototype r1
+
+**Scope:** `core/`, `app/`, `app/run/`, `app/render/`, `harness/`, `demos/*.dem`, `data/*.json`, `tools/*.sh` in the odin-prototype worktree, against `_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/architecture/odin-architecture-v1.md` (§4–§11; ODN-1..18, E1–E32) and the Perkins r1 pitfall list (`_bmad-output/perkins/packet-plumber-prototype-build/r1/consolidated.json`).
+**Method:** exhaustive path walk of every branch/boundary in scope; only UNHANDLED paths reported. Every finding re-verified against disk (file reads + line numbers); crash-class candidates empirically checked with scratch programs outside the repo (no project code modified).
+**Baseline verified:** `odin test core` → 30/30 green; goldens + T1 manifests present for all 6 demos (surge_basics 3000 ticks = win at surge end; error404 250 ticks = run lost — both consistent with ended-stop stepping); shipped demos' capture times are all frame-aligned at logic_hz 10.
+**Empirical results:** (a) Odin nil-map assignment auto-allocates → `app.autopilot_wired` never-`make`'d is SAFE (candidate rejected); (b) `log_read` on a 24-byte corrupt log returns `ok=false` cleanly, but a forged record count of 0xFFFFFFFF attempts the full ~10² GB `make` BEFORE any validation (macOS overcommit masked it) → kept as W4.
+
+## Priority-area status
+
+| Priority area | Status |
+|---|---|
+| core/flow.odin (lifecycle, severance reroute, pool caps, queue depth) | findings (N1–N7) |
+| core/topology.odin (demolish cascade, port limits, span) | findings (W5, W6) |
+| core/demand.odin (growth fallbacks) | findings (W7, N8) |
+| core/health.odin (win/lose/grace boundaries) | findings (W1, N9) |
+| harness/ (demo parser, golden compare, replay) | findings (B1, W2, W3, W10, W11, N12–N16) |
+| core/serialize.odin (binary log round-trip) | findings (W4, N11) — **the round-trip itself is otherwise CLEAN** (writer/reader symmetric, LE, versioned; fingerprint covers ALL sim state incl. packets/rng/events — Perkins #9 verified closed) |
+
+**Explicitly clean (walked, no unhandled paths found):** core/rng.odin (degenerate span guarded, vectors pinned), core/events.odin (append-only, tick-tagged), core/command.odin + core/types.odin (pure data), core/snapshot.odin (bounds guarded, stale-route render fallbacks present), core/qos.odin (largest-remainder/ties/zero-cap pinned by tests), app/audio.odin (constant inputs, failure guarded by `audio_ok`), app/main.odin input paths (onboarding consume, ended-restart, drag release — Perkins #13 verified fixed), demos/*.dem (well-formed at hz 10), tools/*.sh (build/lint; one gate blind spot folded into W9).
+
+## Perkins r1 claim verification (claims checked against disk)
+
+**Verified fixed:** #4 upgrade validate=charge delta (topology.odin:267-272) · #5 upgrade span check (topology.odin:260-262) · #6 ghost-pipe cascade collects by incidence (topology.odin:280-296) · #7/#8 logic_hz single source → ms_per_tick (flow.odin:82, catalog.odin:317-320) · #9 fingerprint covers in-flight packets+latency+rng+events (serialize.odin:96-180) · #10 replay keystone is packet-rich with guards (determinism_test.odin:81-86) · #11 apply_tick=next-tick pinned on both paths (app/run/run.odin:82-97, core/run.odin:117-135) · #13 onboarding consumes the click (app/main.odin:117-124) · #21 integer isqrt span (topology.odin:79-104) · #23 emphasis preset from balance.json (flow.odin:403-406) · #27 surge accumulators reset on new surge (health.odin:38-42) · #28 queue-drop newest-first comment matches code (flow.odin:419-424) · #36 scripted plan draws zero rng (demand.odin:7-10) · #45 bootstrap stats from catalog (run.odin:50-60) · #47 terminal↔terminal rejected (topology.odin:179) · #1/#2 health + QoS behavior tests exist (health_test/qos_test/flow_test) · #46 latency-tolerance defer is explicitly acknowledged (flow.odin header) — accepted defer, not a gap.
+
+**Still open (carried into this build):** #20 strain/critical lead ticks loaded-never-applied (→ N10) · #25 E6 never-drop lane guard absent (→ N2) · #29/#30 batch validate-then-apply staleness (→ W6).
+
+---
+
+## BLOCKER
+
+### B1 — Mis-sized or corrupt golden silently PASSES the T2 pixel compare
+- **location:** harness/goldens.odin:91-93 (`compare_images` returns `-1, 0, {}` on size mismatch) + harness/goldens.odin:79-86 (`check_golden` fails only `if mismatch > 0`)
+- **trigger_condition:** golden PNG rendered at a different resolution, truncated/corrupt PNG (`rl.LoadImage` yields width 0), or any decode failure — `mismatch == -1` is not `> 0` and falls into the pass branch
+- **potential_consequence:** the regression net reports T2 green against a broken or missing-comparable golden; visual regressions ship undetected — the harness's core promise ("zero-tolerance compare") inverts exactly when the golden is damaged
+- **guard_snippet:** `if mismatch != 0 { fail } // treat -1 (size/decode mismatch) as failure, and check golden.data != nil after LoadImage`
+
+---
+
+## WARNINGS
+
+### W1 — One healthy tick fully refills the grace window (never-lose exploit); E30 hysteresis absent
+- **location:** core/health.odin:64-70 (`else { h.in_grace = false; h.grace_ticks_left = bal.grace_window_ticks }` on the first non-breach tick)
+- **trigger_condition:** rolling uptime oscillating across `win_uptime_pct` — each single healthy tick resets the 200-tick grace countdown to full before it can expire
+- **potential_consequence:** under flapping SLA the grace window never empties, the meter never drains, and a chronically degraded run is practically unlosable; E30's enter/exit-threshold hysteresis has no catalog fields and no implementation at all
+- **guard_snippet:** refill grace gradually (e.g. +1 tick per healthy tick, capped) or require a sustained recovery window; add enter/exit thresholds per E30
+
+### W2 — Harness tick/frame quantization: crash for logic_hz > 60, wrong sim rate for hz ∤ 60
+- **location:** harness/main.odin:169 (`frames_per_tick := FRAME_HZ / int(catalogs.balance.logic_hz)`) + harness/main.odin:203 (`frame % i64(frames_per_tick)`)
+- **trigger_condition:** catalog-legal `logic_hz` values (validation only requires `> 0` and dividing 1000): hz ∈ {100, 125, 200, 250, 500, 1000} → `frames_per_tick == 0` → **modulo-by-zero trap**; hz ∈ {25, 40, 50} → truncated frame divisor → sim runs at 30/60/60 Hz against a demo timeline authored in wall-ms
+- **potential_consequence:** harness crash or silently mistimed demos (expect windows, captures, and run length all skew from the scripted ms) on a balance retune that the catalog validator explicitly allows
+- **guard_snippet:** at harness start: `if FRAME_HZ % hz != 0 || hz > FRAME_HZ { fatal("logic_hz must divide 60 for the virtual clock") }` (or accumulate rational frames)
+
+### W3 — Capture times not floor-to-frame quantized (spec §10.3); non-aligned times silently never capture
+- **location:** harness/main.odin:235-241 (`if cap_ms == ms` where `ms := frame * 1000 / FRAME_HZ`)
+- **trigger_condition:** `capture at 130ms` — `floor(130×60/1000) = 7`, but `ms` only takes values `frame*1000/60` (…116, 133…), so 130 never equals any `ms`; intents DO floor (`it.frame = ms*60/1000`), captures don't
+- **potential_consequence:** a demo author gets zero captures and zero error for a legal-looking capture time; shipped demos only pass because all times are multiples of 1000 ms
+- **guard_snippet:** quantize at parse: `cap_frame := ms * FRAME_HZ / 1000` and compare frames, or emit "capture time not frame-aligned" at parse
+
+### W4 — `log_read` trusts the record count: giant pre-allocation before any bounds sanity check
+- **location:** core/serialize.odin:292-293 (`n := r_u32(&r); cmds := make([]Command, n, allocator)`)
+- **trigger_condition:** corrupt/crafted log with a huge count field (verified: 0xFFFFFFFF → a ~10² GB `make` attempt precedes record decoding; short buffers then decode-clean to `ok=false`, but the allocation itself is unbounded)
+- **potential_consequence:** process abort/OOM on strict-overcommit platforms instead of the defined `ok=false` rejection — the "binary log round-trip" trust boundary
+- **guard_snippet:** `if int(n) > (len(r.data) - r.pos) / 9 { return {}, nil, false } // 9B = smallest record`
+
+### W5 — `pipes_between` counts past its output buffer; `compute_route` slices `pair_buf[:cnt]` unguarded
+- **location:** core/topology.odin:145-156 (`n += 1` even when `n >= len(out)`) + core/flow.odin:250-253 (`pair_buf[:cnt]` with `pair_buf: [MAX_ROUTE]u32`)
+- **trigger_condition:** >32 parallel live pipes between one node pair — today port caps (≤16) make it unreachable via validated commands, but a junction with `port_capacity: 0` (= unlimited, the terminal convention) or a future router with >32 ports opens it
+- **potential_consequence:** runtime bounds trap (or OOB read under `-no-bounds-check`) inside the deterministic core; harness `resolve_pipe_ref` has the same shape with an 8-slot buffer (demo_parse.odin:196-204)
+- **guard_snippet:** `cnt = min(cnt, len(pair_buf))` at every `pipes_between` call site (or have `pipes_between` stop counting at `len(out)` like `neighbors` does)
+
+### W6 — `topology_apply_all` (the E23 authority) validates against pre-batch state; intra-batch staleness corrupts or over-spends
+- **location:** core/topology.odin:336-348 (validate-all loop uses the same `budget`/topology snapshot, then applies sequentially) + apply-side map reads without `ok` (topology.odin:244)
+- **trigger_condition:** (a) one batch with two draws each ≤ budget but summing > budget → both pass → budget goes negative; (b) a batch `demolish(node X)` + `draw(X, Y)` → X validates against pre-batch state, then `t.node_by_id[X]` misses at apply → slot 0 → **pipe drawn to node slot 0** (silent wrong-node mutation); Perkins r1 #29/#30 carried
+- **potential_consequence:** negative budget and/or silently corrupted topology from the spec'd batch path; production replay currently dodges it only because `step` applies per-command (run.odin:122-135) — the E23 proc itself remains the trap for any future caller
+- **guard_snippet:** validate each command against the running state/budget inside the batch (as `step` does), or re-validate between applies; add `sa, ok := t.node_by_id[c.a]` guards in `apply_command`
+
+### W7 — Last-resort growth scan strands spawns off-network (E31 violation)
+- **location:** core/demand.odin:142-148 (the min-dist-only scan drops the `growth_spawn_near_junction` requirement that `pos_free` enforces at demand.odin:117-128)
+- **trigger_condition:** crowded map — every position within 12 Manhattan of a junction fails min-separation, but min-dist-satisfying positions exist far from all junctions (plausible late-run: 13 nodes, 3 junctions on a 40×30 grid)
+- **potential_consequence:** a terminal spawns beyond every tier's `max_span` (18) of all routers → unconnectable demand → unwinnable pressure — the exact "house 20+ tiles from every router" failure the header claims the build avoids
+- **guard_snippet:** keep a connectability requirement in the last-resort scan (within some tier's span of a live junction), else fail the spawn with an event rather than strand it
+
+### W8 — Catalog range-validation gaps (ODN-5 fail-fast): truncation, wrap, dead content, zero-world
+- **location:** core/catalog.odin — `jint` float/i64→i32 truncation (398-403); balance block defaults without range checks (317-336); optional `growth_box`/`map` objects (327-335); no duplicate-id check anywhere
+- **trigger_condition (each verified against the code path it reaches):** `1.5` or `> 2³¹` JSON numbers silently truncate (`case json.Float: return i32(x)`); negative `start_tick`/`growth_first_tick` wrap through `u64(...)` to ~never-fire (demand.odin:59); `queue_drop_depth ≤ 0` → every packet sheds instantly (flow.odin:416-424); `packet_pool_cap 0` → no spawns ever (flow.odin:324); `meter_start_pct ≤ 0` → Run_Lost on tick 1 (health.odin:88-92); `volume ≤ 0` demand silently skipped (flow.odin:286-288); duplicate entry ids shadow silently (`class_index` first-match); missing `"map"` → zero world → `view_compute` scale = win/0 (view.odin:39-47); missing `"growth_box"` → zero box → corner spawn at {0,0} via the last-resort scan (demand.odin:142-148)
+- **potential_consequence:** malformed-but-parseable data produces a silently broken/absurd sim instead of a named startup error — the ODN-5 contract
+- **guard_snippet:** per-field range rules at load (positive depths/caps/meters/spans, non-negative ticks, reject Floats and i32 overflow, require `map`+`growth_box`, reject duplicate ids and non-positive volumes)
+
+### W9 — Bootstrap/testkit discard catalog lookup `ok` — renamed ids silently map to index 0
+- **location:** core/run.odin:56-58 (`host, _ := node_type_index(...)`) + core/testkit.odin:16,61,75-76 (`wide, _ := tier_index(...)`)
+- **trigger_condition:** a `node_types.json`/`pipe_tiers.json`/`packet_types.json` rename (e.g. `router_mid` → `router_m`) — lookup returns (0, false), the discard keeps 0, and the boot map/autopilot silently builds with type/tier/class 0
+- **potential_consequence:** unwinnable boot topology or wrong-tier autopilot wiring with zero error — a §7.1 "no dropped errors" violation the lint gate misses (tools/lint.sh gate 4 only greps single `_ =`, not multi-assign discards)
+- **guard_snippet:** check each `ok` and raise the critical-error path; extend gate 4 to `, _ :=` discards of fallible lookups
+
+### W10 — `harness replay` passes vacuously: prefix-only compare, missing manifest OK, era unchecked
+- **location:** harness/replay.odin:85-94 (`for i in 0 ..< min(len(golden), len(hashes))` then prints OK, exit 0) + replay.odin:69-94 (`if os.exists(man_path)` skips all comparison when absent) + replay.odin:36-46 (catalog_hash/logic_hz checked, `header.era` never)
+- **trigger_condition:** (a) a log whose replay produces fewer hashes than the manifest (early end, truncated log) → only the prefix compares; (b) a typo'd demo arg → `goldens/<arg>.t1` doesn't exist → no comparison at all → "OK (deterministic re-sim)", exit 0
+- **potential_consequence:** the ODN-11 replay contract reports success having verified nothing (or only a prefix) — silent divergence ships as green
+- **guard_snippet:** require the manifest, compare `len(golden) == len(hashes)`, fail on either; validate `header.era` against the run's era
+
+### W11 — `map bare` (and any unknown fixture) silently ignored: every demo gets the six-node bootstrap
+- **location:** harness/main.odin:158 (`if demo.map_fixture != "bare"` only skips name aliases) + harness/demo_parse.odin:33-35 (any fixture string accepted) + app/run/run.odin:50 (`run_context_create` → `run_init` always bootstraps)
+- **trigger_condition:** `map bare` in a demo — the parser's own Demo doc comment offers "bare" as a fixture, but there is no bare-run path; the full six-node map spawns regardless
+- **potential_consequence:** a demo authored for an empty map silently runs on the bootstrap map — wrong scenario, wrong goldens, no error
+- **guard_snippet:** honor "bare" via `run_init_bare` in the harness create path, and reject unknown fixture names at parse time
+
+---
+
+## NOTES
+
+### core/flow.odin
+- **N1 — Pool-cap drop ignores the E22 lane ladder.** flow.odin:324-330: on `len(f.packets) >= packet_pool_cap` the *incoming* spawn drops regardless of class/lane; the spec's "drop lowest-priority lane first" ordering (E22/ODN-8 "BE-first") is absent — an Express surge spawn can drop while Best-effort packets hold slots. Near-unreachable in PROTO (per-lane queue depth 60 sheds long before the 6000 cap). Guard: on cap, evict/deny by lane BE → Standard → Express.
+- **N2 — E6 quantum floor and E7 WRR floor absent; MAX_WEIGHT bound missing.** flow.odin:396-445 uses `qos_allocate` caps directly: no never-drop lane floor at quantum 1 (spec §6.3 pins a min-capacity test), no serialization window with a ≥1-slot floor — a positive-weight lane gets cap 0 when `capacity < 3` or weights are skewed on narrow pipes (e.g. `{1,1,100}` on cap 5 → caps `{0,0,5}`) → its packets are never served and shed at queue depth. `validate_command` also lacks the spec'd `0 ≤ w_i ≤ MAX_WEIGHT` bound (topology.odin:204-207; arithmetic itself is i64-safe). No PROTO class is never-drop and shipped presets never zero a lane on shipped tiers — latent. Guard: floor the never-drop lane at 1 unit post-allocation in lane order; add the weight bound.
+- **N3 — Over-long/oversize topology degrades to misattributed `.Unreachable`.** flow.odin:252 + 219-231: paths needing > MAX_ROUTE(32) edges → `route_len = 0` → spawn dropped with reason `Unreachable` although a route exists (SLA harmed as if unroutable); `nb_buf: [64]u32` / `path_buf: [64]u32` silently truncate >64-degree nodes / >64-node maps the same way (flow.odin:198-231). PROTO ≤ 13 nodes — latent. Guard: distinct drop reason or explicit map-size assertion.
+- **N4 — Severance reroute falls back to the packet's origin when an earlier edge died in the same cascade.** flow.odin:259-269 (`current_node` returns `node` unchanged when a *completed* edge's pipe is gone) + flow.odin:447-463: an E27 junction demolish kills the pipe *behind* an in-flight packet too → reroute computes from `p.src` — the packet restarts from its source with latency intact (teleport-back) instead of rerouting from its true position per E1. Bounded (re-traverse or Severance drop). Guard: anchor at the far endpoint of the last surviving completed edge, or drop as Severance when the anchor chain is broken.
+- **N5 — Unguarded degenerate inputs in helpers (all callers currently guard).** flow.odin:118-134 `weighted_pick([])` → `items[rng_range(rng, 0, -1)]` → OOB (rng_range's degenerate-span return makes it `items[0]` on an empty slice); flow.odin:149-163 `rr_next(n = 0)` → modulo-by-zero. Latent landmines if a future caller forgets the guard. Guard: `if len(items) == 0 { return 0 }` / `if n <= 0 { return 0 }`.
+- **N6 — E28 asymmetry: no-terminal demand feeds no strain.** flow.odin:291-297: when a role has no terminals, demand accrues `demand_seen` + `report.unmet` but never enters `dropped`/the rolling uptime window, while the route-failure path (flow.odin:314-322) counts as a full loss — spec says undelivered demand "feeds strain exactly like a loss". Latent in PROTO (roles always present). Guard: accrue `acc.dropped += volume` (and `tick_drop`) on the no-terminals path.
+- **N7 — `balance.rolling_window_ticks` is dead data.** flow.odin:17 + push_rolling (506-517) use the full hardcoded `ROLLING_MAX = 128` arrays; the catalog value (100) is loaded (catalog.odin:330) but applied nowhere, and the comment's "must be <= this" rule is enforced nowhere — retuning the window silently does nothing. Guard: size the window from the catalog with a `<= ROLLING_MAX` load-time check.
+
+### core/topology.odin / core/demand.odin / core/health.odin / core/crisis.odin
+- **N8 — Growth stall retries full scans every tick, silently.** demand.odin:89-95: `next_growth_pos` failure leaves `growth_next` untouched → the row-major + last-resort scans rerun every tick forever, and the whole role queue stalls behind the failed spawn (no event/metric). Guard: advance `growth_next` (or emit a growth-stalled signal) on failure.
+- **N9 — Zero-traffic surge auto-wins; unmet excluded from the win metric.** health.odin:78-84: `total == 0` → `uptime` defaults to 100 → `Ev_Run_Won`; `report.unmet` is never added to `surge_dropped` (health.odin:44-45), so demand that never spawned can't count against the win. Latent in PROTO (immortal host/houses + volume > 0 guarantee spawns every surge tick). Guard: treat `total == 0` as neutral (no win) and fold unmet into the loss side.
+- **N10 — surge_active is one bool across set-pieces; crises.json never parsed; lead-time tunables dead (Perkins #20 carried).** crisis.odin:75-83: resolving one of two overlapping set-pieces clears `surge_active` (snapshot `surge_active`/`surge_ends_in` desync — latent with the single shipped set-piece). `crises.json` is hashed (catalog.odin:127,145) but never parsed/validated — fail-fast absent and `preventive_redesign` copy is unread (the HUD toast is hardcoded, app/main.odin:339); `root_cause.node = 0` is the documented map-wide sentinel (events.odin:54-56) — acceptable. `strain_lead_ticks`/`critical_lead_ticks` load (catalog.odin:324-325) into nothing. Guard: count active set-pieces; parse crises.json in `catalogs_load`; wire or remove the lead tunables.
