+# Verification-Gap Review — Odin + Raylib Packet Plumber prototype (r1)
+
+**Scope:** the fresh Odin build in this worktree (`core/`, `app/`, `harness/`, `demos/`,
+`data/`, `tools/`, `.github/workflows/ci.yml`). Question: what behavior could regress
+*without reliable verification catching it*?
+
+**Method (what was actually checked):**
+- Read end-to-end: all of `core/` (incl. all 30 `@(test)` bodies), `app/`, `harness/`,
+  all 6 demos, the `.t1` manifests, `ci.yml`, `tools/*.sh`, architecture
+  `odin-architecture-v1.md` (esp. §10 harness, §11.7 E1–E32), and the Perkins r1
+  findings (`consolidated.json`, 47 findings).
+- Ran the full verification surface twice — `odin test core` (30/30 green) and
+  `tools/harness.sh run` (6/6 demos green, stable across runs). `tools/lint.sh` green.
+  `odin build app` succeeds (verified — CI never builds it).
+- Ran `harness replay` on all 6 shipped `.log.bin` files (results quoted below).
+- Ran a scratch probe (`/tmp/pp-probe`, imports `core` read-only) to empirically check:
+  (a) whether warning events fire inside the goldened runs; (b) QoS work-conservation;
+  (c) pool-exhaustion reachability; (d) the second-surge accumulator reset;
+  (e)–(g) whether the E1 severance test actually exercises the severance machinery.
+  Repo code was not modified.
+
+Findings are graded **blocker / warning / note** per review instructions.
+
+---
+
+### T2 pixel compare silently passes when the golden is undecodable or the wrong size
+
+- **Grade: blocker**
+- **Changed surface:** the T2 zero-tolerance pixel compare — `harness/goldens.odin:90-93`
+  (`compare_images` returns `mismatched = -1` on any dimension mismatch) consumed at
+  `harness/goldens.odin:79-87` (`if mismatch > 0 { fail } else { pass }`).
+- **Impacted consumer or site:** every T2 golden check — all 13 captures across the 6
+  demos (`check_golden`, `harness/goldens.odin:70`), i.e. the entire pixel tier that
+  CI gates on (`tools/harness.sh run` in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`).
+- **Existing test evidence:** the harness is the verification; nothing tests the
+  comparator. I read `check_golden`/`compare_images` fully. raylib's `LoadImage`
+  returns `Image{0}` (width 0) on decode failure — confirmed in the pinned vendored
+  source (`tools/raylib-sw/src/src/rtextures.c:263-266`). So two reachable cases both
+  yield `mismatch == -1`, which fails the `> 0` test and is treated as a match:
+  (a) a corrupt/undecodable golden PNG on disk (bad merge, LFS-pointer file, truncated
+  checkout); (b) any framebuffer/golden dimension drift (e.g. someone edits the
+  `rl.InitWindow(1280, 720, ...)` at `harness/main.odin:104`).
+- **Missing verification:** a dimension/validity guard that fails loudly —
+  `if mismatch != 0` (treat `-1` as mismatch), or an explicit
+  `golden.width != img.width || golden.height != img.height` failure before comparing.
+- **Demonstration:** replace `goldens/boot/01000ms.png` with a text file, or change
+  the harness window to 640×360. Every demo's T1 still passes (sim untouched) and every
+  T2 compare returns `-1` → `else` branch → PASS. `harness run` exits 0; CI is green
+  while T2 verifies nothing.
+- **Consequence:** the pixel tier — the build's only visual regression net — can be
+  fully disarmed by a corrupted artifact or a one-line window-size change, with a green
+  run.
+- **Suggested test shape:** one-line fix plus a harness self-check: run mode should fail
+  when a golden file exists but doesn't decode, or when dimensions differ. (Fits the
+  repo's own style: the "no golden" case at `harness/goldens.odin:71-75` already fails
+  loudly — extend the same treatment to "golden unreadable/wrong-sized".)
+
+### `harness replay` verifies only a prefix of the manifest, prints "OK", and nothing runs it
+
+- **Grade: blocker**
+- **Changed surface:** the ODN-11 replay path — `harness/replay.odin:49`
+  (`total := last_tick + 120`), `:85` (compares only `min(len(golden), len(hashes))`
+  ticks), `:92,102` (prints "manifest-matched" / "OK" unconditionally after the prefix
+  compare). The binary round-trip itself: `core/serialize.odin` `log_write`/`log_read`.
+- **Impacted consumer or site:** the save/validation artifact contract
+  (architecture §10.3 "Demos lower to action logs… replays reproduce the run
+  bit-for-bit"; §11.4). The blessed artifacts `goldens/*.log.bin` are written at
+  `harness/main.odin:288-290` and consumed only by `harness/replay.odin:21`.
+- **Existing test evidence:** searched the repo for `log_write`/`log_read` — the only
+  callers are those two harness sites; no `@(test)` exercises the binary round-trip
+  (the determinism keystone reuses the *in-memory* action log, never the serialized
+  bytes — `core/determinism_test.odin:79`). `ci.yml` runs only `odin test core` +
+  `tools/harness.sh run`; `replay` appears in no CI step and no script default.
+  Measured what replay actually verifies today (all printed "OK"):
+  - `error404`: manifest-matched through **121 of 250** ticks — the run_lost terminal
+    at tick 250 is never re-simulated.
+  - `surge_basics`: matched through **2501 of 3000** ticks — the surge end and run_won
+    at tick 3000 are never re-simulated.
+  - `flow_basics`: 121/300. `qos_dial`: 127/200. Only `boot` (50/50) and
+    `draw_and_reject` (30/30) compare the full manifest.
+- **Missing verification:** (a) replay must simulate to the manifest's recorded tick
+  count (the `ticks N` header is parsed-and-discarded at `harness/goldens.odin:213-215`;
+  replay could read it) — a run whose terminal event lands after `last apply_tick + 120`
+  is currently declared OK without its decisive ticks ever being re-simulated;
+  (b) any automated invocation — a CI step or a check inside `harness run` that the
+  blessed `.log.bin` still round-trips to the blessed `.t1`.
+- **Demonstration:** hand-edit `goldens/error404.log.bin` to truncate it after the
+  header, or let `log_write`/`log_read` drift by one field: `harness run` and
+  `odin test core` stay green (neither reads the file), CI stays green, and even a
+  manual `harness replay error404 …` prints "manifest-matched through 121 ticks / OK"
+  for a log that never reaches the loss. The `replay_error` latch (ODN-11 "critical")
+  likewise can't fire for ticks the replay never runs.
+- **Consequence:** the ODN-11 keystone claim ("the binary format makes 'identical' a
+  `mem.compare`") is unverified where it matters: the saved-log artifact can be stale,
+  truncated, or format-drifted, and the terminal states of the two fun-gate demos are
+  never proven reproducible from their logs. A save/replay regression ships silently.
+- **Suggested test shape:** drive replay length from the manifest's `ticks` header (or
+  store the run's end tick in the log header), fail when the compared prefix is shorter
+  than the manifest, and add `harness replay` per demo to CI (or fold a
+  log-round-trip assertion into `harness run` after the T1 compare).
+
+### The E1 severance test never puts a packet on the pipe it demolishes
+
+- **Grade: blocker**
+- **Changed surface:** the E1 reroute-or-drop machinery — the severed-pipe pass in
+  `core/flow.odin:447-462` (reroute from current node, else `drop_packet(.Severance)`).
+- **Impacted consumer or site:** `test_severance_reroute_or_drop`
+  (`core/flow_test.odin:118-175`), the test named as the E1 pin (and cited as closing
+  Perkins r1 "Demolish-in-transit reroute/severance untested").
+- **Existing test evidence:** I read the test and then measured it. Reproducing its
+  exact fixture (seed 1337, same draws, same plan) in a scratch probe: at the demolish
+  tick, **0 packets have the direct leg as their current edge**, and **0 Severance
+  events fire** in the 40 ticks after. This is structural, not bad luck: packets
+  complete an uncongested edge within the tick they enter it (spawn → same-tick serve,
+  `flow.odin:405-436`), so a packet's *current* edge at an inter-tick boundary is only
+  ever a congested pipe — and the test's wide pipes never congest. The test's assertion
+  (`delivered_after > delivered_before`, `flow_test.odin:171-174`) is satisfied by
+  newly spawned packets routing via the pre-built alternative path (BFS preferred the
+  direct leg before the demolish; new spawns use j2 after it) — no reroute or drop need
+  ever occur. Counter-probe with a *congested* leg (same flood as the QoS test):
+  53 packets on the demolished pipe → 103 Severance drops — the machinery works when
+  actually exercised; the shipped test just never exercises it.
+- **Missing verification:** an assertion that the demolished pipe carried in-flight
+  packets at demolish time (e.g. count `p.route[p.edge_idx] == pipe` > 0) and that
+  either a reroute occurred (packet survived with a new route) or an
+  `Ev_Packet_Dropped{reason: .Severance}` was emitted. The drop-with-no-alternative
+  branch (`flow.odin:459-461`) has no assertion anywhere — `Severance` appears in the
+  test suite only in a comment (`core/flow_test.odin:120`).
+- **Demonstration:** delete the entire severed-pipe pass at `core/flow.odin:447-462`
+  (or break the reroute, or change the drop reason): all 30 tests still pass — the
+  fixture's deliveries continue via j2 — and all 6 goldens stay green (no demo
+  demolishes a pipe under load). E1 fully regresses with every gate green.
+- **Consequence:** the contract the build advertises as verified ("Demolish pipe w/
+  packets in transit → reroute or drop w/ `severance` reason") is pinned by a test that
+  cannot fail. A genuine problem noticed while tracing: the same "quiet-pipe" shape
+  means `draw_and_reject.dem`/any demo never goldens a mid-flight demolish either.
+- **Suggested test shape:** congest the target pipe first (the existing flood pattern
+  from `test_qos_priority_protects_its_class`), assert non-zero occupancy of the pipe
+  before demolishing, then assert reroute (alt path present) and
+  `Ev_Packet_Dropped{.Severance}` (alt path absent) as two cases.
+
+### The spec'd work-conserving QoS (gap-fill + WRR floor) is not what runs — and the goldens pin the deviation
+
+- **Grade: blocker**
+- **Changed surface:** link serialization — `core/flow.odin:389-436`: each lane is
+  hard-capped by `qos_allocate` (`cap <= 0 → packet waits`, `:423`); unused capacity in
+  other lanes is never redistributed, and there is no round-robin floor for a zero-cap
+  lane. The spec carried "verbatim": "weight-only allocation; **gap-fill at
+  serialization; WRR floor**; largest-remainder integers" (`odin-architecture-v1.md`
+  §11.2, also §6.3, ODN-3, and E7's mechanism note "WRR floor in `qos_serialize`
+  + test", §11.7).
+- **Impacted consumer or site:** every contended link in every run; the verification
+  surface that blesses the behavior is `test_qos_priority_protects_its_class`
+  (`core/flow_test.odin:88-115`) plus the T1 goldens of all 6 demos.
+- **Existing test evidence:** the QoS tests pin the *allocator* (largest-remainder,
+  all-zero fallback, tie order — `core/qos_test.odin`) and one direction of relative
+  delivery under the emphasis preset. No test asserts gap-fill (idle-lane capacity
+  usable by a busy lane) or a floor for a zero-share lane; `grep` finds no
+  `Queue_Overflow`/starvation assertion beyond the flood test's "Best-effort must not
+  starve" — which passes because the shipped presets allocate ≥1 unit to every lane on
+  the shipped tiers, not because a floor exists. Empirical probe: one dialed wide leg
+  (40 u/s, emphasis {4,1,1} → caps {27,7,6}) carrying an email-only flood of 20/tick
+  for 40 ticks delivered **exactly 240** (6/tick — the strict Best-effort cap) with the
+  Express lane 100% idle; a work-conserving serializer would approach 800.
+- **Missing verification:** a test that idles the promoted lane and asserts the
+  demoted class exceeds its strict share (gap-fill), and a test with a
+  zero-allocating weight set (e.g. {10,1,1} on a capacity-5 narrow pipe → Best cap 0)
+  asserting the lane still drains (WRR floor). Note the second case is currently
+  unreachable from any shipped surface: `Cmd_Set_Lane_Weights` has no UI, no demo
+  intent (see the parser finding), and no test drives it — the E6/E7 zero-lane corner
+  exists only via hand-crafted replay logs.
+- **Demonstration:** the strict partition is baked into all 6 T1 manifests and 13 T2
+  goldens — they were generated by it. If anyone now implements the spec'd gap-fill,
+  `harness run` fails on every contended demo and the "fix" looks like a regression;
+  conversely the current behavior (a dialed 40 u/s pipe throttling lone traffic to
+  6 u/s) passes every gate today.
+- **Consequence:** a headline differentiator behavior (FORGE #4 — the dial decides who
+  suffers) ships in a shape the architecture says it shouldn't have, and the golden
+  harness — the build's regression net — actively locks the wrong shape in.
+- **Suggested test shape:** unit-level `flow_step` scenarios in `core/flow_test.odin`
+  mirroring the probe above (idle-lane gap-fill; zero-share floor), then a deliberate
+  re-bless if the spec is amended to strict partition instead.
+
+### Scripted captures and intents are never audited — a capture that never fires fails nothing
+
+- **Grade: warning**
+- **Changed surface:** demo execution — `harness/main.odin:183` (`captures_done`
+  recorded, never reconciled), `:235-249` (capture only when
+  `frame * 1000 / 60 == cap_ms` exactly), `:158-176` (intents applied only while
+  `frame <= total_frames`).
+- **Impacted consumer or site:** all 6 demos' T2 coverage and intent scripts.
+- **Existing test evidence:** I read the loop; the shipped demos' times all land
+  cleanly (verified: every capture in `demos/*.dem` is a multiple of 250 ms, and
+  `frame*1000/60` hits them; every intent is well inside its `run`). But: (a) capture
+  times that no frame maps to (e.g. `capture at 17ms` — `frame*1000/60` is never 17)
+  silently never fire, while *intents* quantize differently (`floor(ms*60/1000)` —
+  `harness/demo_parse.odin:87`), so 17 ms works as an intent and vanishes as a capture;
+  (b) an intent past `run_ms` is silently never applied; (c) in `save` mode a skipped
+  capture silently writes no golden, and a later `run` only fails on a *missing* golden
+  if the capture fires — so a stale/orphaned golden for a no-longer-fired capture time
+  is never compared again.
+- **Missing verification:** an end-of-run reconciliation: every scripted capture fired
+  (`len(captures_done) == len(demo.captures)`), every intent was applied
+  (`intent_idx == len(demo.intents)`), fail otherwise.
+- **Demonstration:** edit `boot.dem` to `capture at 17ms`: `harness run` stays green
+  (zero T2 checks execute), and `harness save` blesses nothing — the demo now has no
+  pixel coverage and no gate notices. Same for appending `at 99999ms draw_pipe …`.
+- **Consequence:** demo edits that intend visual or interaction coverage can silently
+  reduce it to nothing; goldens left behind by renamed demos rot unexamined.
+- **Suggested test shape:** the reconciliation check above, plus parser rejection of
+  capture times that don't land on a frame (or adopt the same floor-to-frame rule as
+  intents and assert uniqueness after quantization).
+
